      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding `walk_deps` directly to `dep_map_` breaks `root_targets` computation in `Analyzer::Analyze()` (lines 336-340) when `additional_compile_targets` includes `\"all\"`:\n\n```cpp\nfor (const auto* item : all_items_) {\n  if (item-\u003eAsTarget() \u0026\u0026 dep_map_.find(item) \u003d\u003d dep_map_.end())\n    root_targets.insert(item-\u003eAsTarget());\n}\n```\n\nFor regular `deps`, excluding `A` from `root_targets` when `B` depends on `A` is sound because building `B` in Ninja also builds `A`. However, `G --walk_deps--\u003e A` emits no Ninja edge to `A` (building `G` does *not* build `A`). Marking `A` as non-root in `dep_map_` causes two bugs:\n\n1. **With a cycle** (the motivating JNI Zero pattern: `app -\u003e final -\u003e pickles --walk_deps--\u003e app`): every target in the cycle becomes a key in `dep_map_`, so none of them are added to `root_targets` (unless another top-level target outside the cycle happens to depend on `app`). Modifying a source file under `app` with `\"additional_compile_targets\": [\"all\"]` leaves `outputs.compile_labels` empty and misreports `\"status\": \"No dependency\"` (with `\"compile_targets\": []` when any unrelated root target exists in the build, or `\"compile_targets\": [\"all\"]` if `filtered_targets` is completely empty).\n2. **Even without a cycle**: if a top-level `executable(\"app\")` is referenced by a top-level `generated_file(\"manifest\")` via `walk_deps \u003d [ \":app\" ]` (with at least one other unrelated root target in the build), modifying a source file of `app` returns `\"compile_targets\": [\"//:manifest\"]` and skips compiling `//:app`.\n\nConsider keeping `walk_deps` for reverse affect propagation (`AddAllItemsReferringToItem`), while excluding `walk_deps` edges when determining `root_targets` (e.g., via a separate map or a `has_real_dependents` set), and adding unit tests in `src/gn/analyzer_unittest.cc` covering both the cycle and non-cycle cases.\n\n(Minor nit: `Target::walk_deps()` safely returns an empty vector for non-`GENERATED_FILE` targets via `kEmptyGeneratedFile`, so the `output_type() \u003d\u003d Target::GENERATED_FILE` check could also be omitted to match `validations()` above and `command_refs.cc`.)\n\n*(Note: This draft comment was generated by Jetski.)*",
