      "message": "Because `walk_deps` are designed to allow cycles with `deps` (e.g. `app -\u003e final -\u003e pickles --walk_deps--\u003e app`), running `gn refs \u003cout_dir\u003e \u003ctarget\u003e --tree --all` on a target reachable from such a cycle will infinitely recurse and overflow the stack: `DoTreeOutput()` (lines 173 and 181) passes `seen_targets \u003d nullptr` to `RecursivePrintTargetDeps()` / `RecursivePrintTarget()`, which then has no cycle termination.\n\n(The same latent issue exists for `validations` cycles, though cycles are much more central to `walk_deps`.) Consider tracking the current recursion stack (e.g., an `ancestors` / `current_path` set) even when `seen_targets` is null so `--tree --all` still expands diamonds without infinitely recursing on cycles.\n\n*(Note: This draft comment was generated by Jetski.)*",
